.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH swarm-relay 1  "swarm 0.2.2" "Swarmgit manual"
.SH NAME
swarm\-relay \- Run a relay server for peers that cannot accept connections
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBswarm relay\fR [\fB\-\-listen\fR] [\fB\-\-name\fR] [\fB\-\-allow\-node\fR] [\fB\-\-password\-file\fR] [\fB\-\-key\-file\fR] [\fB\-\-metrics\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-listeners\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-splices\fR] [\fB\-\-listeners\-per\-ip\fR] [\fB\-\-splices\-per\-ip\fR] [\fB\-\-connects\-per\-minute\fR] [\fB\-\-requests\-per\-minute\fR] [\fB\-\-splice\-kib\-per\-sec\fR] [\fB\-\-node\-daily\-mib\fR] [\fB\-\-idle\-secs\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-network\fR] [\fB\-\-public\fR] [\fB\-\-allow\-private\fR] [\fB\-\-round\-secs\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run a relay server for peers that cannot accept connections
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-listen\fR \fI<LISTEN>\fR [default: 0.0.0.0:42425]
Address to listen on
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fI<NAMES>\fR
Name clients dial this relay by, as host:port. Repeatable. A listener\*(Aqs proof is bound to it. Without any, proofs are not bound to a name
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-node\fR \fI<NODE_ID>\fR
Let only this node register. Repeatable. Keeps the relay out of the relay network
.TP
\fB\-\-password\-file\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Require the secret in this file to register or dial. Clients send it only to an address that includes the relay\*(Aqs key, so this needs \-\-key\-file. Keeps the relay out of the relay network
.TP
\fB\-\-key\-file\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Keep the relay\*(Aqs key in this file, created on first use, so that `host:port#key` addresses keep working across restarts
.TP
\fB\-\-metrics\fR \fI<ADDR>\fR
Serve counters over HTTP on this address (off by default)
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-listeners\fR \fI<MAX_LISTENERS>\fR [default: 10000]
Most registered listeners
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-splices\fR \fI<MAX_SPLICES>\fR [default: 500]
Most simultaneous splices
.TP
\fB\-\-listeners\-per\-ip\fR \fI<LISTENERS_PER_IP>\fR [default: 2]
Most nodes registered from one address
.TP
\fB\-\-splices\-per\-ip\fR \fI<SPLICES_PER_IP>\fR [default: 8]
Most splices one dialing address may have open
.TP
\fB\-\-connects\-per\-minute\fR \fI<CONNECTS_PER_MINUTE>\fR [default: 20]
Most connect attempts from one address in a minute
.TP
\fB\-\-requests\-per\-minute\fR \fI<REQUESTS_PER_MINUTE>\fR [default: 120]
Most info and lookup requests from one address in a minute
.TP
\fB\-\-splice\-kib\-per\-sec\fR \fI<SPLICE_KIB_PER_SEC>\fR [default: 8192]
Rate of one splice in KiB per second, 0 for no limit
.TP
\fB\-\-node\-daily\-mib\fR \fI<NODE_DAILY_MIB>\fR [default: 10240]
Most bytes carried for one node in a day, in MiB
.TP
\fB\-\-idle\-secs\fR \fI<IDLE_SECS>\fR [default: 120]
Close a splice after this many idle seconds
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-network\fR
Stay out of the relay network: no DHT announce and no gossip
.TP
\fB\-\-public\fR
This relay is reachable from the internet: announce it without first asking another relay to dial back
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-private\fR
Accept relays on loopback and private addresses, for a closed network
.TP
\fB\-\-round\-secs\fR \fI<ROUND_SECS>\fR [default: 1800]
Seconds between relay network rounds (gossip)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
